    {
      "id": "highlights",
      "heading": "Highlights",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "Understand how to logically group Java files using packages.",
            "Learn to structure large-scale applications by breaking them down into manageable components.",
            "Use packages to improve readability, maintainability, and reusability of your code.",
            "Interface and class files in one package can easily be reused in another by importing."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 47,
      "subsections": [
        {
          "id": "best-practices-for-packages",
          "heading": "Best Practices for Packages",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Use lowercase letters for package names: com.banking.services",
                "Avoid using import package.* — instead, import only needed classes, e.g., import java.util.Scanner;",
                "Group packages by functionality: com.bank.accounts, com.bank.loans, etc.",
                "Create reusable classes/interfaces inside packages to improve consistency and efficiency."
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 37,
          "subsections": []
